    "body": "pulse task #2833 \u00b7 generation 1.\n\n<!-- pulse-operation:c4df8e955e1b319abb16e653524c17e3 -->\n\nassigned to @PORTALSURFER. the frozen task plan is retained in pulse and copied below.\n\n# Pulse task #2833: Use theme orange-red for active device toggles and dark gray for bypass\n\nOperation: c4df8e955e1b319abb16e653524c17e3\nAssignee: PORTALSURFER (Pulse #1, GitHub ID 41680373)\n\nUser requests the shared device on/off (bypass) button be theme orange-red when the device is ON/active, and dark gray when BYPASSED/off. Apply consistently to native device headers for instrument/effect Track and Return chains using existing shared device/control styling. Reuse the actual semantic orange-red accent and dark-gray theme tokens, not hardcoded copied RGB or per-device hacks. State reflects canonical enabled/bypass state, not selection, focus, hover, pointerdown or an inverted bypass boolean. Preserve legible icon contrast, hover/pressed/focus feedback and keyboard accessibility in both states. Do not recolor all parameter switches, change DSP/bypass behavior, default enablement, device selection or on/off hit areas.\n\nCoordinate shared-shell source1 #2829/PR433 thin rounded device outline and #2796/PR402 focus repair; #2799/PR405 selected-device0 toggle remains separate behavior. Real rendered control state should update after click/keyboard action, Undo/Redo and reopened persisted state as existing paths support; proportional shared-widget/production header checks should verify actual active/off painting on representative Track/Return devices and preserve semantic button behavior. No implementation-mirroring-only tests or broad runtime tests for a color-only change.\n\nSource1 is the shared device-panel writer; queue after current coherent essential421/402 checkpoint and implement separate canonical styling PR alongside433 without overlapping source5EQ406 edits. Focused local checks and exact source/evidence handoff to sole merger. In Progress before merge, Ready for Review only after verified canonical merge. Root native visual acceptance separate, no live app actions, installation, forced quit or data changes.\n\ncreated by pulse shared PR intake/start task. builds, checks and merging follow the repository's own instructions.",
